      "content": "To append a new sentence to an existing file in Python, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Open the File in Append Mode**: Use `'a'` as the mode when opening the file. This allows you to add content at the end without overwriting the entire file.\n\n2. **Write the New Sentence**: Utilize the `write()` method of the file object to append the new sentence.\n\nHere is an example code snippet:\n\n```python\nwith open('existing_file.txt', 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    f.write('\\nThis is the new sentence.')\n```\n\n**Explanation**:\n- The `'a'` mode opens the file for appending.\n- `encoding='utf-8'` ensures the file uses UTF-8 encoding, which is widely supported and consistent across systems.\n- The `write()` method adds the new sentence at the end of the file.\n\nThis approach creates a new line after the existing content if the file doesn't exist or appends to it if it does.",
